# Knowledge Base (Corpus)

The corpus is {{ .vars.campaign_name }}'s knowledge base - a searchable collection of documents that agents can reference during work.

## Directory Structure

```
corpus/
├── README.md           # This file
├── documents/          # Source documents
│   ├── guides/         # How-to guides
│   ├── reference/      # Reference documentation
│   └── standards/      # Coding standards, patterns
├── index/              # Search indices (auto-generated)
└── embeddings/         # Vector embeddings (auto-generated)
```

## Adding Documents

### Using the CLI

```bash
# Add a single file
guild corpus add path/to/document.md

# Add a directory recursively
guild corpus add path/to/docs/ --recursive

# Add from URL
guild corpus add https://example.com/docs --fetch
```

### Manual Addition

1. Place documents in `corpus/documents/`
2. Run `guild corpus index` to update the index

## Supported Formats

- Markdown (`.md`)
- Plain text (`.txt`)
- PDF (`.pdf`)
- Code files (`.go`, `.py`, `.ts`, etc.)

## Searching

```bash
# Basic search
guild corpus search "authentication patterns"

# Search with filters
guild corpus search "error handling" --type=go

# Get top results
guild corpus search "API design" --limit=5
```

## Best Practices

### Organize by Topic
```
documents/
├── architecture/
│   ├── patterns.md
│   └── decisions/
├── apis/
│   ├── rest-guidelines.md
│   └── graphql-conventions.md
└── security/
    ├── authentication.md
    └── authorization.md
```

### Use Clear Titles
Documents should have descriptive titles that agents can understand.

### Keep Documents Focused
One topic per document works better than long, multi-topic documents.

### Update Regularly
Remove outdated documents and add new ones as knowledge evolves.

## Integration with Agents

Agents automatically search the corpus when:
- Working on commissions
- Answering questions
- Making architectural decisions

You can also explicitly reference corpus documents in commissions:

```markdown
## References
- [corpus://architecture/patterns.md]
- [corpus://security/authentication.md]
```

## Maintenance

```bash
# Rebuild all indices
guild corpus rebuild

# Check corpus health
guild corpus status

# Remove stale entries
guild corpus clean
```

